{'author': 'Andre Eckstein',
 'description': 'Monitors the members of local groups on Windows hosts, by '
                'default the local Administrators group, and who has '
                'administrative rights on Linux hosts.\n'
                '\n'
                'Linux: the agent plugin local_group_members.py reports the '
                'members of privileged groups (sudo, wheel, ...), the users '
                'and groups in the sudoers files and the accounts with UID 0.\n'
                '\n'
                'Windows: the agent plugin local_group_members.ps1 reads the '
                'members with Get-LocalGroupMember (ADSI fallback) and works '
                'on Windows installations of any language. One service "Group '
                'Membership <name>" per group; the rule "Local group members '
                '(Windows, Linux)" can alert on local users, unwanted members, '
                'members missing from an allow list and changes since the '
                'service discovery. The members are also added to the HW/SW '
                'inventory.\n'
                '\n'
                'Includes an agent bakery rule and plugin (bakery API v2, '
                'Checkmk 2.5) to deploy the plugins and select the groups.\n',
